@startuml 17_seq_undo_redo
!include _style.puml
title Sequence - Undo / Redo
autonumber

actor User
participant "EditorScreen" as E
participant "EditorSession" as S
participant "ToolRegistry" as TR
participant "History" as H
participant "Command" as C
participant "Project" as P
participant "Selection" as Sel

User -> E : Ctrl+Z  (Edit > Undo)   or   Ctrl+Y / Ctrl+Shift+Z  (Edit > Redo)
E -> S : undo()  /  redo()
S -> S : playback.pause()
S -> TR : dispatch(Cancel)   (always; idempotent for idle tools)
note right of TR
  Cancel semantics (04): stroke -> commits what was painted; Move drag -> rolled back (nothing moved);
  rectangle / ellipse / polygon -> discards the preview; Pick / Fill -> nothing to do.
  So the history is complete BEFORE the undo is performed.
end note
alt undo()
  S -> H : undo(project)
  alt undo_stack is empty
    H --> S : None   (menu item is disabled, shortcut does nothing)
  else
    H -> C : pop entry; entry.cmd.revert(project)
    C -> P : restore previous state\n(cells of one layer / frame background / frame list / layer list / layer properties / canvas size / fps)
    H -> H : redo_stack.push(entry)
    H --> S : Some(UndoStep{ label, selection: entry.selection.before })
  end
else redo()
  S -> H : redo(project)
  alt redo_stack is empty
    H --> S : None
  else
    H -> C : pop entry; entry.cmd.apply(project)
    C -> P : re-apply
    H -> H : undo_stack.push(entry)
    H --> S : Some(UndoStep{ label, selection: entry.selection.after })
  end
end
opt UndoStep.selection is Some   (only entries made by Move cells, Paste and Import carry one)
  S -> Sel : restore(selection)   (the marching ants jump back / forward together with the cells; also restores the mask size after a canvas resize)
end
S -> S : thumbnails.retain_only(ids); status bar shows "Undid: <label>" / "Redid: <label>" for 2 s
note over H
  Any NEW command (execute / record_applied) clears the redo stack.
  Zoom, tool, brush and colours are never part of undo. The selection is part of undo ONLY for the entries that carry a SelectionChange.
  Undoing a command always selects the affected frame (and layer) so the user sees what changed.
end note
@enduml
